  "composer": {
    "rawText": "[Title: Static in the Ultraviolet]\r\n[Style: psychedelic rock, clean studio recording, electric guitar (fuzz), bass guitar, drum kit, analog synth pad, confident male vocalist]\r\n[Caption: A drift through distortion and thought.]\r\n[Image: violet fog with blurred neon lights]\r\n[Refresh Title: Purple Haze]\r\n[Theme: Colors]\r\n[Gradients: 2]\r\n[Seed: 41]\r\n[Created: January 26, 2026 at 11:15 AM]\r\n[Composer Version: v1.4]\r\n\r\n[Intro]\r\n[Smooth, exploratory melodic movement.]\r\nThe air is thick with colored sound,\r\nMy feet lift slightly off the ground.\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Grounded melodic contour that develops naturally.]\r\nThe walls all bend, the clocks unwind,\r\nA second sun inside my mind.\r\nI reach for words that slide away,\r\nThey melt like stars before the day.\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Calm melodic progression with slight variation.]\r\nThe mirror hums, it knows my name,\r\nIt smiles but never stays the same.\r\nI breathe in light, I breathe out doubt,\r\nThe edges blur, then fade me out.\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\n[Memorable melodic hook with emotional clarity.]\r\nThis purple haze won’t let me go,\r\nIt pulls me where I don’t yet know.\r\nBetween the truth and what I see,\r\nThe blur feels almost real to me.\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[Focused melodic storytelling with light motion.]\r\nThe city sings in liquid tones,\r\nThrough borrowed thoughts and silent phones.\r\nI’m not lost, I’m just delayed,\r\nInside the mess the mind has made.\r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n[Unexpected melodic turn that feels intentional.]\r\nIf clarity comes crashing through,\r\nI hope it’s strange and slightly blue.\r\nDon’t wake me yet, don’t clear the phase,\r\nI’ve learned to live inside the haze.\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\n[Higher register with expanded phrasing.]\r\nThis purple haze won’t let me go,\r\nIt pulls me where I don’t yet know.\r\nBetween the truth and what I see,\r\nThe blur feels almost real to me.\r\n\r\n[Ending]\r\n[Melody gently resolves with clarity.]\r\nThe colors thin, the echoes stay,\r\nA softer shade to end the day.\r\n",
